  "glossErbarioTerm": "Herbarium",
  "glossErbarioText": "A collection of plants, once dried and annotated on sheets with the date and place of collection. Here it fills up with the species you Meet and study.",
  "glossDesiderataTerm": "Desiderata",
  "glossDesiderataText": "In herbaria and among collectors, the list of specimens one wishes to find. Here, the species you have chosen to look for, as many as you like.",
  "glossErborizzareTerm": "Botanizing",
  "glossErborizzareText": "Roaming fields and woods to observe and study plants: the historical word for botanists' field trips.",
  "glossStazioneTerm": "Station",
  "glossStazioneText": "In botany, the precise place where a population of a species grows, with its soil, exposure and altitude. Here, the spot where you Met a species and where you can return to Draw from it.",
  "glossTrattoTerm": "Trait",
  "glossTrattoText": "A condition of the moment when you Draw an Essence (Full moon, Rain, Fog, Dew…): an Essence carries all of them. Recipes ask for different Traits: the same plant on different days gives different Essences.",
  "glossAttingereTerm": "Draw",
  "glossAttingereText": "Drawing the Essence from a Station without touching the plant: you photograph and observe, you don't pick.",
  "glossMaestriaTerm": "Mastery",
  "glossMaestriaText": "The final Level of a species: you must remember what you learned days later and have Drawn the species in the field under different conditions. It has to be kept: after 30 days without questions about the species it falls dormant, and a short quiz reawakens it.",
